    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nThe fix is complete and verified. The bug was that `frai gate init --ci` wasn't passing the `--ci` flag to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Root cause:** In Commander.js, program-level options (like `--ci` on the main `frai` command) are parsed before subcommands, so the flag was consumed by the main program and never reached the gate command's arguments.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the gate command's action handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Accept the `command` parameter (the third argument in the action handler)\n2. Access parent command options via `command.parent?.opts()`\n3. If `--ci` is set at the parent level, explicitly add it to the arguments passed to frai-gate\n\n**Verification:** After rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n- \u2713 `FRAI-SPEC.md` (the spec template)\n- \u2713 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the GitHub Actions workflow)\n\nThe dist files are built and ready to use.",
